Sri Balaji Tourism 🛕

📽️About the Project

This is my first GitHub project, a tourism website I created while learning web development. The website showcases some popular pilgrimage places in India, including Tirupati, Varanasi, Arunachalam, and Yadadri.

I built this project to practice HTML, CSS, and Bootstrap and to understand how different sections of a website work together.


✨Features

=> A home page with a welcome section.
=> A list of favourite pilgrimage places.
=> Information and images about different destinations.
=> Image carousels to view destination pictures.
=> An embedded video related to Yadadri.
=> Navigation between different website sections.

🛠️Technologies Used

=> HTML
=> CSS
=> Bootstrap
=> JavaScript

📁 Folders

1. Clone this repository:

   git clone https://github.com/Chandrashekar6321/Tourism-Website.git
   
2. Open the project folder.
3. Open `index.html` in your browser.

🌱 What I Learned

While creating this project, I practised writing HTML, styling web pages with CSS, using Bootstrap components, and adding images and interactive elements.

As this is my first project, I learned a lot through practice and found areas where I can improve my web development skills.

🚀 Future Improvements

=> Make the website more responsive on mobile devices.
=> Add more tourist destinations.
=> Improve the design and user experience.
=> Add more interactive features.

